Integer coefficients for the element routines in this addon.

Procedure pointers
------------------

Summary of assignment of user functions/subroutines to procedure pointers:

  coefficients%func => func       ! scalar function for q
  coefficients%vfunc => vfunc     ! vector function for q

  coefficients%func1(1)%p => Iz   ! scalar function for Iz
  coefficients%func1(2)%p => A    ! scalar function for A 
  coefficients%func1(3)%p => Iyy  ! scalar function for Iyy
  coefficients%func1(4)%p => Izx  ! scalar function for Izx
  coefficients%func1(4)%p => J    ! scalar function for J


List of the coefficients
------------------------

1   Component choice parameter in computing a derivative.
    For example coefficient%i(1)=1 means the normal strain in truss_deriv1.
    See the sources for the possibilities in various derivative routines.

2   Numerical integration rule (intrule) for the domain.
    For example with intrule=3 a three-point Gauss-Legendre integration is used.

3   Lateral displacement interpolation (intpolv):
    0: P3 Hermite shape functions
    1: P4 Hermite shape functions

4   The scalar right-hand side q (distributed force) is as follows:
    <0: q=0
    0: constant, given by coefficients%r(4)
    1: given by a function, funcnr=coefficient%i(5)
       NOTE: function func must be assigned to coefficients%func
    NOTE: coefficients%i(4) only available for 1D beam elements.

5   funcnr for the right-hand side

6   Iz: the second moment of area with respect to the neutral (local) z-axis is
    computed as follows:
    0: constant, given by coefficients%r(3)
    1: given by a function, funcnr=coefficient%i(7)
       NOTE: function func must be assigned to coefficients%func1(1)%p
    NOTE: Iz is commonly denoted by just I in 1D and 2D problems. Also Izz.
    NOTE: the (local) x-axis is along the beam.

7   funcnr for Iz

8   A: the cross sectional area of the beam is computed as follows:
    0: constant, given by coefficients%r(1)
    1: given by a function, funcnr=coefficient%i(9)
       NOTE: function func must be assigned to coefficients%func1(2)%p
    NOTE: coefficients%i(8) not available for 1D beam elements.

9   funcnr for A

10  The vector right-hand side q (distributed force) is as follows:
    <0: q=0
    0: constant, given by coefficients%r(5:7)
    1: given by a function, vfuncnr=coefficient%i(11)
       NOTE: vector function must be assigned to coefficients%vfunc
    NOTE: for truss elements only coefficients%i(10)=0 applies, where the
          force generated by constant distributed load is equally
          transferred to the two end nodes.
    NOTE: coefficients%i(10) not available for 1D beam elements.

11  vfuncnr for q

12  Axial displacement interpolation (intpolu):
    0: default value = 2
    2: P1
    6: P2
    NOTE: coefficients%i(12) not applicable for 1D beam elements.

13  Axial (torsional) rotation interpolation (intpolt):
    0: default value = 2
    2: P1
    6: P2
    NOTE: coefficients%i(13) only relevant for 3D beam elements.

14  Iyy: the second moment of area with respect to the neutral (local) y-axis is
    computed as follows:
    0: constant, given by coefficients%r(11)
    1: given by a function, funcnr=coefficient%i(15)
       NOTE: function func must be assigned to coefficients%func1(3)%p
    NOTE: coefficients%i(14) only relevant for 3D beam elements.

15  funcnr for Iyy

16  Izy: the second product of area with respect to the neutral (local) z and
    y-axis is computed as follows:
    0: constant, given by coefficients%r(12)
    1: given by a function, funcnr=coefficient%i(17)
       NOTE: function func must be assigned to coefficients%func1(4)%p
    NOTE: coefficients%i(14) only relevant for 3D beam elements.

17  funcnr for Izy

18  J: the polar second product of area is computed as follows:
    0: constant, given by coefficients%r(13)
    1: given by a function, funcnr=coefficient%i(19)
       NOTE: function func must be assigned to coefficients%func1(5)%p
    NOTE: coefficients%i(15) only relevant for 3D beam elements.

19  funcnr for J

20--100 Reserved for future use. Set to zero for future compatibility.


